  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1230 AM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Continued dry with warming temperatures through the \nweek.\n\nA strengthening 1035mb Canadian high will continue to dominate the \nregional weather pattern as it shifts east across the Midwest to the \nmid-Atlantic this week. Meanwhile a positively titled upper trough \nover the eastern US will give way to a strengthening upper-level \nridge, and an upper-level shortwave will migrate from the southern \nPlains toward the northeast Gulf by the end of the week. The strong \nridging and subsidence will keep things dry for several more days, \nwhile temperatures slowly moderate each day in a reactively \nunchanged weather pattern.\n\nThe only significant forecast challenge comes late next weekend as \nthe aforementioned upper wave lingers over the Gulf and Florida, \nresulting in cyclogenesis and the potential for a low pressure \nmoving north near the NC coast.  The last few runs of the GFS track \nthe low north into the Carolinas, but the ECWMF and consensus of AI-\nbased models keep the low at or well east of the NC coast. Even \nthose solutions closer to the coast yield only light QPF in interior \nNC. Thus the current official forecast leans to the drier solutions, \nbut there is at least a scenario where a system brings some much \nneeded rain to the area.",
